e, the value $x=\\pi -1$ is not in the domain of the function." 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268525 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268526 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268527 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268528 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268529 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1041 "selection" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268525 13194139533954 true] [17592186268524 1110 #uuid "56c0d3d5-f743-56c7-81d9-b3ab67669797" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268525 1034 "\\pi -1" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533954 true] [17592186268525 1111 #uuid "d1ab3020-87b3-5b63-a9f6-3fcabcaf9121" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268526 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533954 true] [17592186268526 1111 #uuid "6ae5298a-9001-5266-9eff-50afbca8463e" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268527 1034 "3-\\pi " 13194139533954 true] [17592186268527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533954 true] [17592186268527 1111 #uuid "e0bcd112-71aa-54aa-bcca-271e4a37fb0e" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268528 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533954 true] [17592186268528 1111 #uuid "48a594f3-8bbd-593b-92a9-7ce1bd7c74c2" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268529 1034 "\\pi -3" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533954 true] [17592186268529 1111 #uuid "4992a1b1-a44c-53f0-b1c2-58d84af1f3cb" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268531 13194139533954 true] [17592186268530 1089 "q-70714" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533954 true] [17592186268530 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\n- $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n- $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n- $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268530 1113 #uuid "a72ce64f-755c-5a29-9c7b-cd49fb251531" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268530 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$  does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$  does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$" 13194139533954 true] [17592186268531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268532 13194139533954 true] [17592186268531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268533